Kapow!

01:05:45.810 --> 01:05:50.790
That little weenie digivolves on his own, and Renomon stays the same even with two modified cards.

01:05:51.770 --> 01:05:53.670
What does that gogglehead have that I don't?

01:05:53.890 --> 01:05:54.010
Huh?

01:05:54.300 --> 01:05:55.320
This is ridiculous.

01:05:56.360 --> 01:05:58.100
You'd better digivolve soon, Renomon.

01:05:58.280 --> 01:05:59.980
I'm not going to be threatened by some over...

01:06:05.860 --> 01:06:16.750
You must be very tame-able. Look at them, they come ra-

01:06:17.410 --> 01:06:22.440
Look, new Modify cards. Here, you can have this lame one. I don't need it.

01:06:24.110 --> 01:06:25.370
What are training grips?

01:06:25.920 --> 01:06:29.360
Sheesh, don't you know anything? They make your rookie big and strong.

01:06:29.500 --> 01:06:29.980
So you can-

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:31.040
and stomp out the enemy.

01:06:31.280 --> 01:06:32.680
It's like resistance training.

01:06:32.840 --> 01:06:34.860
You probably won't use it, but maybe you can get

01:06:34.860 --> 01:06:36.300
some sucker to trade for it.

01:06:36.480 --> 01:06:37.120
Yeah, sure.

01:06:38.270 --> 01:06:40.310
Just what I need, another useless card.

01:06:45.460 --> 01:06:47.310
Sir, I've detected another one.

01:06:47.660 --> 01:06:49.910
Well, what are you waiting for?

01:06:50.430 --> 01:06:51.510
Yes, sir, right away.

01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:54.320
Pin-pointing tracer coordinates.

01:06:58.000 --> 01:06:59.460
Never learn, do they?

01:07:08.030 --> 01:07:11.670
Sometimes I think Kazu gives me these cards so he can use them against me later.

01:07:12.620 --> 01:07:14.240
You give him way too much credit.

01:07:14.770 --> 01:07:16.050
Yeah, I gotta work on that.

01:07:17.760 --> 01:07:18.320
What's up?

01:07:18.660 --> 01:07:20.850
Your ears?

01:07:21.030 --> 01:07:21.530
Oh no!

01:07:21.710 --> 01:07:22.190
What's that?

01:07:22.760 --> 01:07:24.360
I hope it's not what I think it is.

01:07:24.570 --> 01:07:25.110
Me too!

01:07:25.630 --> 01:07:26.710
What do you think it is?

01:07:27.350 --> 01:07:29.410
Whatever it is, it's coming right at us!

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:32.760
Something just might be right.

01:07:33.820 --> 01:07:34.620
Come on!

01:07:34.980 --> 01:07:36.970
Oh, this is some way for having...

01:07:38.330 --> 01:07:39.840
Must run faster!

01:07:40.140 --> 01:07:42.180
I could if Terrier Mom wasn't choking me.

01:07:50.680 --> 01:07:51.640
Digital field!

01:07:51.760 --> 01:07:53.460
This just keeps getting better and better.

01:07:53.990 --> 01:07:56.310
What is a digital field and why is it chasing us?

01:07:56.430 --> 01:07:58.170
You picked a dumb time to ask questions.

01:07:58.520 --> 01:07:59.760
For once, I agree with you.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:00.420
Thank you.

01:08:02.990 --> 01:08:04.090
We'll never outrun it!

01:08:04.250 --> 01:08:05.870
Oh man, this thing is fast!

01:08:06.130 --> 01:08:06.790
We'll have to split up!

01:08:06.950 --> 01:08:07.690
You take the bridge!

01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:08.030
Right!

01:08:08.570 --> 01:08:08.730
Thank you.

01:08:08.980 --> 01:08:09.220
Yeah.

01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:11.860
See you on the other side.

01:08:13.500 --> 01:08:14.240
You have to let out.

01:08:14.740 --> 01:08:15.240
Here I am!

01:08:17.850 --> 01:08:18.610
It's after you!

01:08:19.390 --> 01:08:20.490
Keep running!

01:08:21.080 --> 01:08:23.560
I'll go get Guillaumon and be back as soon as I can.

01:08:28.800 --> 01:08:29.940
You're just full of ideas!

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:35.020
I suppose Momentai isn't really appropriate now, huh?

01:08:41.300 --> 01:08:41.940
Tamer.

01:08:42.350 --> 01:08:43.330
Just a suggestion.

01:08:44.590 --> 01:08:46.530
How about suggesting a better place to hide?

01:08:48.800 --> 01:08:53.980
What's the status of the anomaly?

01:08:55.120 --> 01:08:55.840
Bio-emerging.

01:09:30.120 --> 01:09:34.600
Let's see, Gorillamon, he's a beast Digimon, champion level.

01:09:35.790 --> 01:09:37.290
Gorillamon, it's been a long time.

01:09:39.470 --> 01:09:41.730
Gorillamon, don't you remember me?

01:09:42.120 --> 01:09:43.560
Yeah, Henry, what are you doing?

01:09:43.780 --> 01:09:45.440
We played the game together.

01:09:47.490 --> 01:09:53.190
Listen to me, I won't let Terriermon fight you, so just leave him alone.

01:09:53.450 --> 01:09:54.510
This isn't the game.

01:09:55.180 --> 01:09:56.720
The remember's all right.

01:10:00.540 --> 01:10:29.980
guys have met before. Go back to the other side! Don't think he's listening! Look, I did it! Nooo! Terriormon, don't! I-

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:31.760
I told you before, I don't want you to fight!

01:10:31.860 --> 01:10:33.360
Go back to Gorillamon!

01:10:33.620 --> 01:10:35.500
Um, he does have a point, you know.

01:10:35.820 --> 01:10:38.280
I think I've had enough fun now.

01:10:38.480 --> 01:10:39.390
Hey, people!

01:10:45.600 --> 01:10:47.320
Close! That's one way to put it.

01:10:51.670 --> 01:10:55.100
Warrior Mon!

01:11:00.280 --> 01:11:00.500
See you tomorrow!

01:11:30.090 --> 01:11:31.310
It's the new Digimon game.

01:11:31.700 --> 01:11:33.020
Yep, hot off the press.

01:11:33.100 --> 01:11:35.060
I had to wait in line for hours to get it.

01:11:35.680 --> 01:11:37.510
Thank you, Dad. You're the best!

01:11:37.770 --> 01:11:40.390
Wow, the installation took forever.

01:11:40.650 --> 01:11:43.500
No wonder. Look at all these new options.

01:11:46.180 --> 01:11:49.080
Alright, now who will I play first?

01:11:49.540 --> 01:11:51.870
One that's got a lot of power like Gorillamon?

01:11:51.950 --> 01:11:55.320
Ah, that's boring. Anyone can win with a big Digimon.

01:11:55.540 --> 01:11:58.090
Now Terriermon, that's a challenge.

01:11:58.450 --> 01:11:59.970
He's small and smart, like a...

01:12:01.950 --> 01:12:03.710
He dances like me, too.

01:12:06.970 --> 01:12:09.940
Whatever he said, he didn't mean it.

01:12:11.440 --> 01:12:13.100
Way to go, Guillaumont!

01:12:13.140 --> 01:12:18.680
Down, shut down!

01:12:23.540 --> 01:12:25.540
Close the game, why is it still running?

01:12:26.850 --> 01:12:27.570
Ram frozen?

01:12:30.670 --> 01:12:35.260
Wait, maybe Digimon have a reality outside the game.

01:12:35.810 --> 01:12:38.500
But that just isn't possible, is it?

01:12:45.030 --> 01:12:47.120
This is really weird.

01:12:47.340 --> 01:12:54.560
You must have crossed over from the other side.

01:13:00.860 --> 01:13:01.620
I brought him here.

01:13:01.820 --> 01:13:03.060
It's all my fault.

01:13:03.860 --> 01:13:04.840
Thank you.

01:13:11.350 --> 01:13:12.150
They're forming their data!

01:13:17.370 --> 01:13:18.050
Stop it!

01:13:18.670 --> 01:13:19.490
Carriermon, look out!

01:13:22.810 --> 01:13:25.770
He's totally out of control. How's Terrier Mon supposed to beat him?

01:13:26.100 --> 01:13:26.940
He's too small.

01:13:33.450 --> 01:13:34.210
What should I do?

01:13:34.980 --> 01:13:36.080
Modify cards!

01:13:36.580 --> 01:13:38.640
Terriormon, it's time to make you faster!

01:13:39.020 --> 01:13:39.980
Speed activate!

01:13:40.400 --> 01:13:41.480
Digi-modify!

01:13:42.760 --> 01:13:45.560
It better give you some more strength. You're gonna need it. Power activate!

01:13:45.960 --> 01:13:47.120
Digi-Modify!

01:13:51.430 --> 01:13:51.630
Yeah.

01:13:53.640 --> 01:13:56.220
Way to use your head, Terriormon. He's down for the count.

01:13:56.710 --> 01:13:59.090
Alright, now it's time to sharpen up that aim of yours.

01:13:59.290 --> 01:13:59.990
Targeting activa-

01:14:01.080 --> 01:14:08.600
Almost there. All you need is a little more energy to finish him off.

01:14:08.760 --> 01:14:11.670
Stamina activate. Digi-modify.

01:14:14.400 --> 01:14:15.520
Digi-pollution.

01:14:43.530 --> 01:14:43.910
I do th-

01:15:00.060 --> 01:15:03.160
Gargaman, what are you doing? You've already beaten him, just let him go!

01:15:04.360 --> 01:15:06.200
You're just like all the rest of them.

01:15:07.030 --> 01:15:09.070
I have no idea who you even are anymore!

01:15:09.430 --> 01:15:12.400
What have I done? It's all my fault!

01:15:13.750 --> 01:15:14.490
Carry on!

01:15:16.150 --> 01:15:16.990
You okay?

01:15:17.710 --> 01:15:19.180
Look out!

01:15:20.160 --> 01:15:21.460
I'll distract him for you!

01:15:21.800 --> 01:15:22.120
Hey!

01:15:22.660 --> 01:15:29.970
He's gone too-

01:15:30.380 --> 01:15:32.260
Time to do what I should have done in the beginning.

01:15:32.500 --> 01:15:33.220
Power activate!

01:15:33.800 --> 01:15:34.820
DIGIMONICOR!

01:15:36.000 --> 01:15:36.420
Oh, my God.

01:15:37.220 --> 01:15:37.400
Thank you.

01:15:38.540 --> 01:15:38.940
Wow.

01:15:39.270 --> 01:15:39.930
Bye bye!

01:15:44.740 --> 01:15:45.400
He's too strong.

01:15:46.120 --> 01:15:48.700
Interior mine's just too small to do any real damage.

01:15:49.260 --> 01:15:50.760
But if he did evolve, then we...

01:15:50.760 --> 01:15:51.860
I won't let him!

01:15:52.200 --> 01:15:52.640
Henry?

01:15:53.480 --> 01:15:53.880
Why not?

01:15:54.020 --> 01:15:54.680
You

01:15:57.580 --> 01:15:59.920
You see, when a Digimon beats an opponent in battle,

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:01.520
They absorb the loser's data.

01:16:01.890 --> 01:16:03.950
That's just one of the ways they get more powerful.

01:16:04.580 --> 01:16:05.900
It's just how the program works.

01:16:07.540 --> 01:16:10.140
Son, I think you're taking all this a little too seriously.

01:16:10.800 --> 01:16:13.800
Digimon can't actually get hurt because they don't really exist.

01:16:14.200 --> 01:16:15.080
It's a game.

01:16:16.140 --> 01:16:19.720
Yeah, they're just a bunch of zeros and ones, right?

01:16:21.650 --> 01:16:22.750
Digimon don't exist.

01:16:22.750 --> 01:16:23.710
It's only a game.

01:16:24.050 --> 01:16:27.810
It doesn't matter if they get hurt because they're not real.

01:16:29.360 --> 01:16:29.980
But look at...

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:31.780
Hey Adam, it does matter.

01:16:33.050 --> 01:16:36.500
Carrier Mon, I'm sorry, I didn't mean it.

01:16:43.570 --> 01:16:46.280
Hey, what's this blue card?

01:16:47.000 --> 01:16:48.860
Carrier Mon, hang on!

01:16:49.000 --> 01:16:49.760
Did you modify?

01:16:51.060 --> 01:16:51.620
Nice?

01:17:00.410 --> 01:17:01.050
But how?

01:17:01.410 --> 01:17:12.720
Look what I've done to you.

01:17:15.470 --> 01:17:18.560
Those other Digimon in the game, I hurt them too.

01:17:26.120 --> 01:17:27.160
That's kind of cold.

01:17:28.660 --> 01:17:29.300
Terrier-mon.

01:17:30.030 --> 01:17:31.190
I'm so sorry.

01:17:31.910 --> 01:17:33.060
W-what for?

01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:36.720
I'll never make you fight again.

01:17:36.840 --> 01:17:39.760
Hey! Don't cry. I'm fancy.

01:17:48.200 --> 01:17:49.520
Can't break my promise.

01:17:49.740 --> 01:17:51.080
What if I lose him?

01:17:51.940 --> 01:17:52.940
Henry, wake up!

01:17:53.680 --> 01:17:53.900
Huh?

01:17:54.500 --> 01:17:54.920
What?!

01:17:57.470 --> 01:17:58.530
Don't waste any more time!

01:17:58.970 --> 01:17:59.970
Terriormon has got to-

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:01.040
Why did you evolve to Gargaman?

01:18:01.610 --> 01:18:02.970
There's gotta be another way.

01:18:03.230 --> 01:18:03.830
But what?

01:18:04.420 --> 01:18:06.560
These are the only Modify cards I have left

01:18:06.560 --> 01:18:07.640
and they're totally lame.

01:18:08.290 --> 01:18:09.950
I can't believe we're all out of cards.

01:18:10.860 --> 01:18:13.050
Les, of course.

01:18:13.760 --> 01:18:15.040
What, this thing?

01:18:15.220 --> 01:18:15.700
Yes.

01:18:15.980 --> 01:18:17.960
But it's just a training card, what'll that do?

01:18:18.120 --> 01:18:19.500
Just watch and learn.

01:18:20.310 --> 01:18:22.170
Terriormon, time for a little resistance.

01:18:45.850 --> 01:18:47.690
Okay, that's interesting. Now what?

01:18:50.230 --> 01:18:52.130
Will someone please tell me what's going on?

01:19:00.060 --> 01:19:04.160
now I get it with the training grips on his arm's these two tangled up the fight

01:19:31.210 --> 01:19:32.710
He was up, must come down.

01:19:33.000 --> 01:19:33.620
Mm-hmm.

01:19:36.610 --> 01:19:36.950
Huh?

01:19:37.230 --> 01:19:39.010
I don't think he liked the ride.

01:19:42.440 --> 01:19:43.820
One tough monkey?

01:19:51.480 --> 01:19:51.940
Wait!

01:19:53.430 --> 01:19:55.830
Carrier Mon, I don't want you to absorb his data.

01:19:57.500 --> 01:19:59.680
Can I at least do a little victory dance?

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:09.830
So what happened to Gorilla Mun's data? Did it just disappear?

01:20:10.130 --> 01:20:15.360
I'm not really sure, but hopefully you went back to the other side.

01:20:15.770 --> 01:20:29.970
That was amazing. You and Jared-

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:32.560
really make a great combination, you know that?

01:20:33.230 --> 01:20:35.220
Yeah. Thanks, Toccato.

01:20:35.460 --> 01:20:37.570
Why is it in him? He didn't do anything.

01:20:37.890 --> 01:20:39.470
We're a good combination, too.

01:20:39.810 --> 01:20:40.310
Mm-hmm.

01:20:40.770 --> 01:20:42.530
Like peanut butter and bananas.

01:20:42.710 --> 01:20:43.670
You're obsessed.

01:20:43.930 --> 01:20:44.550
Hey, Henry.

01:20:44.890 --> 01:20:45.050
Huh?

01:20:47.660 --> 01:20:48.140
Momentime.

01:20:48.370 --> 01:20:50.250
Toccato, man, I think I'm hungry again.

01:20:50.630 --> 01:20:53.010
Guillemot, for the last time, I'm not a man.

01:20:53.520 --> 01:20:54.840
Forget it. Let's go eat.

01:20:55.090 --> 01:20:55.830
Okay, Toccato.
